neoxify-patch header: ios-memory-gate

The TUN inbound side of the memory-pressure gate in the iOS engine
(plugins/vpn/xray/gate_darwin.go): while the extension's footprint is high,
new TCP connections are refused with a reset (here) and packets that would
open a new UDP flow are dropped (ios-udp-flows.patch, which calls the same
admitting()); new TCP connections are also admitted at no more than 100 a
second. Unbounded before: a flood of new connections reached 107 MiB on
Stealth and 400 MiB on Shadowsocks; iOS kills the extension at about 50 MiB.
Written against xray-core v26.6.27 (45cf2898ab12): proxy/tun/stack_gvisor.go
and a new proxy/tun/neoxify_gate.go. Applied by
apps/mobile/scripts/xray-core-patch.sh, for the iOS build only. Guarded by
TestEngineMemoryBudget (plugins/vpn/xray), 2026-11-18.

--- a/proxy/tun/stack_gvisor.go
+++ b/proxy/tun/stack_gvisor.go
